  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Region 8: mitigating the impact of typhoons on vulnerable populations in the Eastern Visayas region through camp coordination and campmanagement and shelter anticipatory actions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The key objective of the project is to mitigate physical and socioeconomic harms for the most vulnerable population affected by typhoons induced by sudden evacuation in the Eastern Visayas Region. The project focuses on families living in houses made of light materials that are less durable to typhoons and that are located in hazard-prone zones, and also strives to augment the local government&apos;s life-saving measures in response to disasters - namely mandatory pre-emptive evacuation - which will most likely be required for these vulnerable families when potentially destructive typhoons occur. IOM and its Implementing Partners are ensuring that Internally Displaced Persons (IDPs) have access to safe and dignified living conditions at evacuation centres (ECs) at the onset of their pre-emptive evacuation. Through cash-based interventions, IOM is also facilitating immediate access to appropriate materials and tools for IDPs to repair their shelters right after typhoon&apos;s landfall.</narrative>
  </description>
